e concrete maximum number of consecutive loan renewals.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-013\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_error_handling\",\n      \"evidence\": \"validate item eligibility within 2 seconds and issue the loan receipt\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Defines only the successful self-checkout path and omits error handling when item eligibility validation fails or the barcode cannot be read.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-014\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_value_or_unit\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the allowed maximum number of active hold requests\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"References 'the allowed maximum number' without specifying a concrete numeric limit anywhere in the specification.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-015\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"borrow up to 8 physical items simultaneously\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-009\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Conflicts with SD-009, which limits an active Member in good standing to at most 5 physical items checked out simultaneously rather than 8.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-016\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"21 calendar days from the checkout timestamp\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-010\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Conflicts with SD-010, which sets the standard loan duration for circulating print books to 14 calendar days rather than 21 calendar days.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-017\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"self-register online with only an email address and immediately check out physical books without Librarian ID verification\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-001\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Directly contradicts SD-001, which requires a Librarian to create a new Member account only after verifying government-issued photo ID and recording full name, email address, and phone number.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-018\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"remain held indefinitely until the requesting Member explicitly cancels the hold\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-011\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Directly contradicts SD-011, which mandates holding reserved items on the pickup shelf for exactly 72 hours and automatically cancelling uncollected holds thereafter.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-021\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"coordination\",\n      \"evidence\": \"send an overdue email and/or suspend borrowing privileges and/or apply a penalty flag\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Chained 'and/or' connectors make it ambiguous which combination of actions is required when an item becomes 7 days overdue.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-022\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_actor\",\n      \"evidence\": \"shall be reviewed, approved, and recorded\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses passive voice without identifying which actor (e.g., Librarian, Administrator) or system component is responsible for reviewing, approving, and recording fine waiver requests.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-023\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"weak_phrase\",\n      \"evidence\": \"before the due date if appropriate\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The weak phrase 'if appropriate' leaves the dispatch condition subjective and untestable, and 'before the due date' lacks an explicit lead time.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-024\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"tbd\",\n      \"evidence\": \"TBD years\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Contains an unresolved 'TBD' placeholder instead of a defined retention period for payment receipts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-025\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"$1.25 USD per overdue day per item with no maximum cap\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-019\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Conflicts with SD-019, which specifies an overdue fine of $0.50 USD per overdue day per item capped at $20.00 USD per item.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-026\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"renew borrowed items online at any time regardless of any unpaid overdue fine balance\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-020\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Directly contradicts SD-020, which blocks any Member with an unpaid fine balance exceeding $5.00 USD from borrowing or renewing items.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-027\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"terminology\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Patron's active loan count and enforce the 5-item borrowing limit on the Patron profile screen\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-009\",\n        \"SD-015\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses the undefined term 'Patron' inconsistently instead of 'Member' used throughout the SRS (such as SD-009); its '5-item borrowing limit' also conflicts with the 8-item limit stated in SD-015.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-028\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"return search results quickly even when many users are querying\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses unquantified terms ('quickly', 'many users') without specifying a maximum response time or target concurrent user load.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-029\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"weak_phrase\",\n      \"evidence\": \"where possible\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"The weak qualifier 'where possible' makes snippet highlighting discretionary and untestable without defining the exact conditions under which highlighting is required or omitted.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-030\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"sufficient ISBN matching accuracy and acceptable response times\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses subjective, unquantified qualifiers ('sufficient', 'acceptable') without defining measurable accuracy percentages or latency thresholds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-031\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"efficiently process large batch MARC21 files without noticeable system slowdown\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses vague, unmeasurable terms ('efficiently', 'large', 'noticeable system slowdown') without defining file size, throughput, or performance degradation bounds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-032\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_consequence\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the Catalog Service shall detect the active references\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies only that the Catalog Service detects active loans or holds, without defining the required consequence (such as rejecting deletion and returning an error message).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-034\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"tbd\",\n      \"evidence\": \"TBD intervals\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Contains an unresolved 'TBD' placeholder instead of specifying the concrete full database backup schedule interval.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-035\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"important administrative actions in a timely manner and retain them for an appropriate period\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses vague, unquantified terms ('important', 'in a timely manner', 'appropriate period') without enumerating the audited actions, maximum logging latency, or retention duration.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-036\",\n      \"type\": \"incompleteness\",\n      \"subtype\": \"missing_consequence\",\n      \"evidence\": \"the Failover Manager shall log event FAILOVER-01\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Specifies only logging event FAILOVER-01 when the primary database node becomes unreachable, omitting the actual failover/recovery consequence (e.g., promoting a replica, rerouting traffic, or alerting administrators).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-037\",\n      \"type\": \"ambiguity\",\n      \"subtype\": \"vague_term\",\n      \"evidence\": \"adequate transport security and clear error messages\",\n      \"related_ids\": [],\n      \"rationale\": \"Uses subjective, untestable terms ('adequate', 'clear') without specifying required transport protocols (e.g., TLS 1.3) or concrete authentication error message requirements.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-038\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"accept any Member password of at least 8 characters\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-002\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Conflicts with SD-002, which requires Member passwords of at least 12 characters containing uppercase, lowercase, and numeric characters.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-039\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_values\",\n      \"evidence\": \"active for 60 minutes of user inactivity\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-004\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Conflicts with SD-004, which terminates an authenticated web portal session after 15 minutes of user inactivity rather than 60 minutes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"req_id\": \"SD-040\",\n      \"type\": \"inconsistency\",\n      \"subtype\": \"conflicting_rules\",\n      \"evidence\": \"encrypt all Member passwords using reversible AES-256 encryption so Administrators can decrypt and retrieve forgotten passwords\",\n      \"related_ids\": [\n        \"SD-003\"\n      ],\n      \"rationale\": \"Directly contradicts SD-003, which mandates one-way bcrypt hashing (cost factor 12) for all passwords and prohibits storing or exposing plaintext passwords.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n","duration_seconds":152.842726,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":12906,"output_tokens":21545,"thinking_tokens":18370,"cache_read_tokens":0,"total_tokens":34451}}}
